The sulfur in the sample is converted to H₂S, which reacts with iodine:

\[
\mathrm{H_2S + I_2 \rightarrow 2HI + S}
\]

So 1 mol H₂S consumes 1 mol I₂, and since each sulfur atom gives one H₂S, moles of sulfur = moles of I₂ consumed.

First find the initial moles of iodine added:

\[
n(I_2)_{\text{initial}} = 0.01500\,\text{L}\times 0.0320\,\text{mol/L}
= 4.80\times10^{-4}\,\text{mol}
\]

The excess iodine was titrated with thiosulfate:

\[
\mathrm{I_2 + 2S_2O_3^{2-} \rightarrow 2I^- + S_4O_6^{2-}}
\]

Moles of thiosulfate used:

\[
n(S_2O_3^{2-}) = 0.02629\,\text{L}\times 0.0175\,\text{mol/L}
= 4.60075\times10^{-4}\,\text{mol}
\]

Thus excess iodine is half of that:

\[
n(I_2)_{\text{excess}} = \frac{4.60075\times10^{-4}}{2}
= 2.300375\times10^{-4}\,\text{mol}
\]

So iodine consumed by H₂S:

\[
n(I_2)_{\text{consumed}} = 4.80\times10^{-4} - 2.300375\times10^{-4}
= 2.499625\times10^{-4}\,\text{mol}
\]

Therefore moles of sulfur in the sample:

\[
n(S)=2.499625\times10^{-4}\,\text{mol}
\]

Mass of sulfur:

\[
m(S)=n(S)\times 32.06\,\text{g/mol}
\approx 8.01\times10^{-3}\,\text{g}
\]

So the original sample contained about 0.00801 g sulfur, or 8.01 mg.

To find the total length, I first need the number of sodium atoms in the 1.15 mg sample, then multiply by the diameter of one atom because the atoms are lined up side by side.

Mass of sodium:
\[
1.15\,\text{mg} = 1.15\times 10^{-3}\,\text{g}
\]

Molar mass of sodium is about \(23\,\text{g/mol}\), so moles of sodium:
\[
n=\frac{1.15\times 10^{-3}}{23}=5\times 10^{-5}\,\text{mol}
\]

Number of atoms:
\[
N = nN_A = 5\times 10^{-5}\times 6\times 10^{23}
=3\times 10^{19}\,\text{atoms}
\]

Radius of each atom is \(0.2\,\text{nm}\), so diameter is:
\[
d = 0.4\,\text{nm} = 0.4\times 10^{-9}\,\text{m}=4\times 10^{-10}\,\text{m}
\]

Total length:
\[
L = N d = 3\times 10^{19}\times 4\times 10^{-10}
=1.2\times 10^{10}\,\text{m}
\]

Convert meters to miles using \(1\,\text{mile}\approx 1.6\times 10^3\,\text{m}\):
\[
L \approx \frac{1.2\times 10^{10}}{1.6\times 10^3}
=7.5\times 10^6\,\text{miles}
\]

So the correct option is (d).

